# Learning Notes – Sprint 29

## Overview

Sprint 29 focused on maintaining a consistent user experience when the Student Profile is updated and the Eligible Jobs component depends on the changed student information.

## Concepts Learned

- Learned about reactive data in Lightning Web Components.
- Understood how stale data can appear after a Salesforce record is updated.
- Learned how Custom Events can be used to notify a parent component about a successful update.
- Understood the role of a common parent component in coordinating multiple child components.
- Learned how to use `refreshApex()` to refresh wired Apex data.
- Understood how dependent components can be refreshed after a record change.
- Learned that data ownership and refresh behaviour are important parts of application architecture.

## Key Takeaways

- Updating Salesforce data does not always mean that every displayed component automatically refreshes.
- Custom Events can communicate important changes between components.
- A common parent can coordinate communication between sibling components.
- `refreshApex()` can be used to refresh wired Apex data when necessary.
- Components that depend on changed data should be refreshed appropriately.
- Sprint 29 helped improve the consistency of the Student Placement Portal.
